    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0391" n="362" xml:id="pg362"/>

                <head>136. Memorandum From the Director of the National Security Agency (Canine) and
                    Representatives of the Military Services and Joint Chiefs of Staff to Secretary
                    of Defense Lovett<anchor n="1" xml:id="d136-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1952-11-20">November 20, 1952</date></dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Formal Implementation of the Provisions of NSCID No. 9 Revised<anchor
                            n="2" xml:id="d136-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCE</head>
                    <item>Secretary of Defense Memorandum of 4 November 1952,<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d136-f3"/> subject: Interim Implementation of NSCID No. 9
                        Revised</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Pursuant to the requirements expressed in paragraph 3 of the reference, a
                        working group was formed and developed the inclosed directives.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The proposed directives, concurred in by the undersigned, are submitted
                        for your approval.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In accordance with paragraph 1d of the reference, a list of directives,
                        orders, or instructions relating to Communications Intelligence matters
                        issued by any authorities within the Department of Defense inconsistent or
                        at variance with the provisions of NSCID No. 9 Revised or with the proposed
                        implementing directives inclosed herewith will be forwarded as soon as
                        compiled.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed>Ralph J. Canine</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Major General,
                        US Army</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Director, National Security Agency
                        Chairman</hi><lb/><signed>Robinson E. Duff</signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Major General, USA</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Representing the Secretary of the Army</hi><lb/><signed>L.S.
                        Howeth</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Captain, USN</hi><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Representing the Secretary of the
                        Navy</hi><lb/><signed>John B. Ackerman</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Brigadier General, USAF</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Representing the
                        Secretary of the Air Force</hi><lb/><pb facs="0392" n="363" xml:id="pg363"
                        /><signed>Edward H. Porter</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier
                        General, USAF</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Representing the Joint Chiefs
                        of Staff</hi></closer>




                <xi:include href="d136-a1.xml" xpointer="d136-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d136-a2.xml" xpointer="d136-a2"/>
